# radarr.rules

See core.rules for documentation standards.

## Purpose
Handles movie download automation and tracking through Radarr.

## Trigger Conditions
- User approves a recommended movie.
- User manually requests a title via GUI.
- Overseerr request is approved.

## Metadata Required
- title
- year
- TMDB ID
- quality profile
- minimum availability (e.g., released)
- root folder path
- monitored (bool)
- tags (optional)

## Expected API Usage
- GET /api/v3/movie/{tmdbId} to check existence.
- POST /api/v3/movie to create a new movie entry.
- POST /api/v3/command with "type": "MoviesSearch" to begin search/download.

## Safety Checks
- Verify that Radarr is reachable.
- Avoid duplicates by checking existing movies by TMDB ID or title.
- Ensure quality profile exists in Radarr settings.

## UX Notes
- Confirm title and year before submission.
- Option to auto-search or only add to library.
